 By Neil Irwin and Courtenay Brown &middot; Sep 21, 2026 
 
 
 Global leaders are descending on New York this week for the UN General Assembly before China's leader, Xi Jinping, heads to Washington, D.C., for a state visit that could shape the world's most important economic relationship. More on what to watch below. 

 🤖 Plus: the Federal Reserve's challenge amid more signs the AI buildout is contributing to inflation. Situational awareness: An outside review of the 2023 failure of Silicon Valley Bank, commissioned by Fed vice chair for supervision Michelle Bowman, is out, clocking in at a not-so-brief 365 pages, with further updates and recommendations due out in the months ahead. Read it here .

 Today's newsletter, edited by Jeffrey Cane and copy edited by Carlin Becker, is 1,185 words, a 4.5-minute read. 

 
 
